{
  "$comment": "Relay avatar icon layer on top of relay-avatar.v1.json (that file stays the base: brand -> initial -> generic). Final avatar for a relay connection with a non-empty provider id: (1) stored local choice, if it is one of `icons[].id` -> that icon; if it is \"letter\" -> the initial from the base initial rule (first letter or digit of the trimmed name, else of the host without api./www.; brand matching is skipped), and when there is none fall through to (3); any other value is ignored; (2) base brand match -> brand; (3) default icon = icons[fnv1a32(key) % 10] where key = provider id with ASCII whitespace trimmed and ASCII A-Z lowered (other bytes untouched), hashed as UTF-8 bytes, FNV-1a 32-bit (offset 0x811c9dc5, prime 0x01000193). Empty provider id -> base result unchanged. The choice lives only on this device (never synced); picking the brand cell deletes the stored choice. Picker cells: brand (only when base matched a brand), then the ten icons in this order, then letter (only when the base initial rule yields one). Icons are original glyphs drawn on a 24x24 grid and shipped per end as assets named after `id` (iOS `RelayAvatar/<id>` template images, Android `relay_avatar_<id>` vector drawables, web `relay-avatar-glyphs.generated.ts`), filled / stroked with one color from `palette` (dark 400 / light 600 tokens) where layer opacity 0.4 carries the shading; no plate, no frame. Case id is used as RELAY-AVATAR-ICON-<id> in all ends.",
